---
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { release } from '../../data/release';
---

<DocumentLayout
  route="privacy"
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy and translation data"
  description={`What deepK ${release.version} sends when it translates, and what it keeps on your Mac.`}
>
  <section>
    <h2>The deepK operator does not collect translation content</h2>
    <p>
      deepK provides no feature for its operator to collect, store, or view your source text,
      images, recognized text, or translations. User content is excluded from analytics and
      automatic diagnostic reports, and no translation history is sent to the operator.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Screen Recording is used to read your selected region</h2>
    <p>
      To translate text in images or games that cannot be copied, deepK takes one screenshot of the
      rectangle you explicitly select. It does not record video or continuously monitor the screen.
      Ordinary text and clipboard images do not need this permission. OCR runs on your Mac; only
      recognized text goes to your chosen provider. Loading an original X image makes a request to
      its image server.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Source text is sent to the AI provider you choose</h2>
    <p>
      deepK uses the official CLI installed on your Mac to send the translation instructions and the
      source text to the Codex or Claude Code provider. How the provider handles and retains that
      information follows your account and the service's policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      With Codex, the global instructions in <code>~/.codex/AGENTS.md</code> on your Mac may be
      included in requests if that file exists. Do not put sensitive information in your global
      instructions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Translations stay in memory for a short time</h2>
    <p>
      The ordinary text translation cache holds up to 32 results for 5 minutes in app memory and
      clears when the app restarts. Images and their results stay in the memory needed to display
      and process the current translation window. No content history is sent to the operator.
      Anything you copy or insert into another app follows that app and the macOS clipboard.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Check sensitive text before translating</h2>
    <p>
      Some content that password managers mark as a sensitive copy is blocked. deepK cannot protect
      copies that are marked late or not marked at all, or text pasted directly into the translation
      window.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before sending, check that the text does not contain passwords, tokens, confidential company
      information, or other people's personal information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>External connections on this site</h2>
    <p>
      The home page's translation window plays prepared examples inside your browser without
      requesting a translation. Fonts are requested from Google Fonts, and download and issue links
      go to GitHub.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="website-analytics">
    <h2>Website statistics are measured only if you allow them</h2>
    <p>
      If you allow statistics on the official home, setup, and privacy pages, Google Analytics 4
      counts visits, opening install guidance, successful copies of the Homebrew command, and ZIP
      download clicks. This analytics tool is not added to the translation app. Source text, images,
      OCR text, translations, input fields, clipboard content, and screen recordings are excluded.
      Design previews and editable demo pages are excluded too.
    </p>
    <p>
      No Google Analytics script or measurement request is sent before you allow it. Your choice is
      remembered in this browser for up to 180 days and can be withdrawn below in
      <strong>Website analytics settings</strong>. Measurement is disabled when the browser's Do Not
      Track or Global Privacy Control preference is detected. Once allowed, a fixed source category
      is also kept for the tab session so internal navigation is not counted as a new referral. It
      is cleared when you withdraw consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once allowed, Google may process visitor cookies, device and browser information, and
      approximate location. Page addresses sent by this site are limited to fixed public paths
      without query strings or fragments; referrer addresses are reduced to their origin. Ad
      personalization, Google Signals, User IDs, and automatic form collection are not used.
      Google's processing and retention follow its policies. Web hosting and external links have
      separate access records regardless of this choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Consent and tracking blockers affect visitor counts. Download clicks do not prove installation
      or app use. These statistics help improve acquisition and setup guidance.
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google Privacy Policy ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Reporting issues and third-party notices</h2>
    <p>
      When you report an issue, please describe the steps to reproduce it without source text,
      credentials, or personal information. You do not need to attach real source text or login
      files. Send vulnerability details through private vulnerability reporting rather than public
      issues.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`${release.repositoryUrl}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Report an issue ↗
      </a>{' '}
      ·{' '}
      <a
        href={`${release.repositoryUrl}/security/advisories/new`}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Report a vulnerability privately ↗
      </a>{' '}
      ·{' '}
      <a href={release.noticesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Third-party notices ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocumentLayout>
